    <span class="flow-text"><strong>Core principle from Torah 9:</strong> When praying, speak <em>dibbur emes</em> (a word of truth) &rarr; this is the light of Hashem Himself &rarr; it illuminates the openings through the darkness</span>
  </div>
  <div class="flow-connector">&#8595;</div>

  <div class="flow-step">
    <span class="flow-arrow">&#9654;</span>
    <span class="flow-text"><strong>Two litigants come to court:</strong> one claims falsely &rarr; this is a blemish of <em>emunah</em> (he did not deal faithfully) &rarr; falsehood conceals truth</span>
  </div>
  <div class="flow-connector">&#8595;</div>

  <div class="flow-step">
    <span class="flow-arrow">&#9654;</span>
    <span class="flow-text"><strong>The judge&rsquo;s remedy:</strong> speak only truth, with no inclination &rarr; &ldquo;G-d stands in the congregation of the mighty&rdquo; &rarr; truth (= G-d&rsquo;s light) illuminates who is right &rarr; <em>din emes la&rsquo;amiso</em></span>
  </div>
  <div class="flow-connector">&#8595;</div>

  <div class="flow-step">
    <span class="flow-arrow">&#9654;</span>
    <span class="flow-text"><strong>Three judges = three lines of <em>emes</em></strong> (aleph-mem-sav = beginning-middle-end) = three Patriarchs = Yaakov = truth &amp; judgment &rarr; sustain the three worlds</span>
  </div>
  <div class="flow-connector">&#8595;</div>

  <div class="flow-step">
    <span class="flow-arrow">&#9654;</span>
    <span class="flow-text"><strong>Bribery blinds</strong> &mdash; because without truth there is no light, and without light one cannot see</span>
  </div>
  <div class="flow-connector">&#8595;</div>

  <div class="flow-step">
    <span class="flow-arrow">&#9654;</span>
    <span class="flow-text"><strong>Judgment by day, not by night:</strong> day = <em>emes</em>; night = <em>emunah</em> in smallness &rarr; <em>tzedek</em> + <em>emes</em> = <em>emunah</em> &rarr; evening + morning = &ldquo;one day&rdquo;</span>
  </div>
  <div class="flow-connector">&#8595;</div>

  <div class="flow-step">
    <span class="flow-arrow">&#9654;</span>
    <span class="flow-text"><strong>The judge is called &ldquo;<em>Elokim</em>&rdquo;</strong> &mdash; G-d&rsquo;s light clothes itself in the truthful judge</span>
  </div>
  <div class="flow-connector">&#8595;</div>

  <div class="flow-step">
    <span class="flow-arrow">&#9654;</span>
    <span class="flow-text"><strong>Judges in Eretz Yisroel</strong> = the Land is <em>emunah</em>; <strong><em>P&rsquo;rutah</em></strong> = <em>emunah</em>/<em>t&rsquo;fillah</em> (<em>uf&rsquo;ritah</em>) &rarr; even the smallest monetary blemish requires judicial rectification</span>
  </div>
